      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xsecure__rsa__pss__server__apis_1ga46a9b687574b01d9a3a33e8e0b6db63e" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XSecure_RsaPssSignVerify</definition>
        <argsstring>(const XSecure_RsaPssSignVerifyInput *Input)</argsstring>
        <name>XSecure_RsaPssSignVerify</name>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="struct_x_secure___rsa_pss_sign_verify_input" kindref="compound">XSecure_RsaPssSignVerifyInput</ref> *</type>
          <declname>Input</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function verifies an RSA-PSS signature (SHA3-384) for the given message hash. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Input</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_secure___rsa_pss_sign_verify_input" kindref="compound">XSecure_RsaPssSignVerifyInput</ref> structure</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS - If verification was successful</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_INVALID - On invalid arguments</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_MEMSET_ENC - If signed input data memset fails</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_RSA_ENC - If RSA encryption fails</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_MGF - If mask generation fails</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_SHA - If SHA operation fails</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_BC - If signature trailer byte mismatch</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_MSDB - If masked DB MSB mismatch</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_DB - If DB pattern mismatch</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_HASH_CMP - If hash comparison fails</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_RSA_PSS_ERR_CLEAR - If clearing the local hash buffer fails </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Validate the input arguments</para></listitem><listitem><para>EM must fit hLen + sLen + 0x01 + 0xBC and the caller workspace.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Clear the EM workspace before writing the RSA output.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Recover EM with RSA public-key exponentiation (s^e mod n). The 64-bit API is used so a signature in client DDR is never truncated on a 32-bit PLM.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Rightmost EM octet must be the PSS trailer 0xBC.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Leftmost bits of maskedDB that are outside emBits must be zero.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Split EM: H is the hLen octets before the trailer.</para></listitem><listitem><para>dbMask = MGF(H, maskedDBLen), then DB = maskedDB XOR dbMask.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Clear the leftmost bits of DB that are outside emBits.</para></listitem><listitem><para>PS in DB must be zeros, followed by the 0x01 salt separator.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Hash M&apos; = Padding1 (8 zero bytes) || mHash || salt, then compare H&apos; with H recovered from EM.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Salt is the last sLen octets of DB, after PS || 0x01.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Compare H&apos; against H from EM (double-read against glitching).</para></listitem><listitem><para>Clear H&apos; so it does not remain on the stack. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>        </inbodydescription>
